  "scenario": "Boot the production CCU aperture cache with the standard graphics DTB. Run native KMS, stock Plasma Qt Quick Vulkan, NPU reference compute and network integrity checks.",
  "expected": "Observe 1000 Hz, 2000 ordinary flips with a median near one field, valid stock Qt output, matching NPU tiles and good link integrity.",
  "observed": "The native test delivered 2000 CPU-filled flips in 33.408 seconds and missed 0 fields. Stock Plasma resumed. The steady and resize Qt scenes gave 2393 and 2412 swaps in 60 seconds. They had 1329 and 1284 sampled CRTC FB ID changes over 2000 intervals. The direct PowerVR test drew and submitted 2000 new frames at 56.889 frames/s. It delivered 1889 of 1999 intervals in one field. The separate 120-frame test matched all sampled GPU attachment markers. The NPU matched 24 reference frames. Ethernet and Wi-Fi transferred matching 4 MiB payloads. DRM, display engine and GPU IRQ fault counters remained at zero. In the diagnostic comparison, the median display preparation and DMA sync interval fell from 5.261 to 1.440 ms. The median RCQ verification to provider return fell from 3.106 to 0.581 ms.",
