  "limits": [
    "Native flip pacing used CPU-filled buffers. Qt frameSwapped and sampled CRTC FB ID observe separate software stages. No optical output was measured.",
    "The diagnostic kernel pair measured whole intervals with traces enabled. Production repeats acceptance with the cache but has no diagnostic tracer. Each arm used one boot.",
    "Direct Qt Vulkan enumerated a display and plane but failed when DRM_SET_MASTER returned EACCES for the session user. EGLFS had selected llvmpipe on the diagnostic kernel. These runs give no direct hardware Qt frame rate.",
    "The independent direct PowerVR test renders simple markers. It does not measure Qt Quick or application performance. The earlier experimental E6 native queue reported 119 of 119 one-field intervals on a separate kernel and workload.",
    "Network tests established transfer integrity at the tested links. They did not measure maximum network performance.",
    "The boot log contained one PowerVR DMA map allocation failure for 8192 bytes. Both Qt workloads completed. Their log snapshots showed no additional allocation failures.",
    "A separate experiment prepared the next GPU frame during the previous display request and also tested Vulkan display acquisition. The board stopped answering over both network connections before the logs were collected. The failing stage and the desktop recovery status at the end of this experiment are unknown."
  ],
